meta {
  name: Waiting for you
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_my_actions
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~status: done
  ~project: PROJ-0029
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("each action has cta and status", function () {
    res.body.message.forEach(function (a) {
      expect(a.cta).to.be.oneOf(["upload", "sign_off", "mark_done"]);
      expect(a.status).to.be.oneOf(["open", "done"]);
      expect(a.urgency).to.be.oneOf(["emergency", "urgent", "normal", "low", null]);
    });
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Actions the ERPGulf team assigned to this user: open ones, or finished ones (the last 30 days, or all of one project's).

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_my_actions`  
  **Screens:** Waiting on you, Implementation → Tasks tab

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only this user's actions, for the user's own client company.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `status` | string | no | `done` | `open` (default) or `done`. `done` with `project` returns **every** finished action for that project; `done` without `project` returns actions finished in the last 30 days. |
  | `project` | string | no | `PROJ-0029` | Only this project's actions. Use it when Waiting on you is opened from a project. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:** open actions are sorted by due date, earliest first. Done actions are sorted by `completed_on`, newest first.

  ```json
  {
    "message": [
      {
        "name": "12glqu2bo8",
        "text": "Upload VAT registration certificate and CR copy",
        "due": "2026-11-10",
        "days_left": 4,
        "urgency": "normal",
        "project": "PROJ-0029",
        "cta": "upload",
        "reference": { "doctype": "Project", "name": "PROJ-0029" },
        "status": "open",
        "completed_on": null
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  **Fields:**

  - `name`: send this as `todo` to Complete Action or Upload Action Attachment.
  - `text`: what we're asking for, plain text.
  - `due`, `days_left`: due date and days until it. `days_left` is negative when overdue, and null for done actions. Both are null when the action has no due date.
  - `urgency`: `emergency`, `urgent`, `normal` or `low` (`normal` by default). Null when not set.
  - `project`: the project the action belongs to. Can be null.
  - `cta`: which button to show:
    - `upload` → Upload, opens Upload Action Attachment
    - `sign_off` → Sign off, opens Milestones at the milestone in `reference`. Only Client Admins get these: a milestone sign-off action can't be assigned to a Client User.
    - `mark_done` → Mark done, calls Complete Action
    - `review` is no longer sent: review-type actions come as `mark_done`.
  - `reference`: the record the action is about, e.g. `{ "doctype": "Payment Milestone", "name": "s6ri3u6d64" }` for a sign-off. Can be null.
  - `status`: `open` or `done`.
  - `completed_on`: when it was finished (date-time with offset). Null for open actions. For actions finished before 11 Nov 2026 it falls back to the action's last change, so it is approximate.

  **Tasks tab summary ("2 of 6 tasks done"):** call with `status=done` and with `status=open`, both with `project`. Done = length of the done list (all of the project's finished actions, no 30-day limit); total = done + open.

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`; auth errors raised by Frappe don't.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: `project` isn't this client's project.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **417** `invalid_parameter`: `status` isn't `open` or `done`.

  **Notes:**

  - Empty open list: show "Nothing needed from you right now".
}
